 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "La -s de la tercera persona",
    "@en": "The -s of the third person"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Con **he**, **she** e **it**, el verbo lleva **-s**: **I work** → **he works**; **I live** → **she lives**.",
     "@en": "With **he**, **she** and **it**, the verb carries **-s**: **I work** → **he works**; **I live** → **she lives**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "En muchos verbos se añade **-s**. Si acaban en -s, -sh, -ch, -x u -o, se añade **-es**: finish → **finishes**, watch → **watches**, go → **goes**. Si acaban en consonante + **y**, cambia a **-ies**: study → **studies**.",
     "@en": "In many verbs **-s** is added. If you end up in -s, -sh, -ch, -x u -o, add **-es**: finish → **finishes**, watch → **watches**, go → **goes**. If you end up in consonant + **y**, change to **-ies**: study → **studies**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Have** es irregular: **he has**.",
     "@en": "**Have** is irregular: **he has**."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Negar y preguntar con he y she",
    "@en": "Deny and ask with he and she"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "La negación se hace con **doesn't** y el verbo **sin -s**: **He doesn't work**.",
     "@en": "Denial is made with **doesn't** and the verb **sin -s**: **He doesn't work**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "La pregunta, con **does**: **Does she work?** — **Yes, she does** / **No, she doesn't**.",
     "@en": "The question, with **does**: **Does she work?**-**Yes, she does** / **No, she doesn't**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "La -s se la lleva el auxiliar (do**es**), así que el verbo se queda como está.",
     "@en": "The -s is taken away by the assistant (do**es**), so the verb stays as it is."
    }
   ]
  },
